Z||000000||JohnnyK||04-02-2001||03:02 PM||||I finally got around to sitting down, and actually WATCHING this film.. And now i"m more confused than ever...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> So there was this monolith on the earth, which helped the monkeys evolve.. It somehow dissapears and no one finds it. Another one shows up on the moon, and points us towards jupiter. We go there, and find another one floating in space. and THEN, there is an 60's light show, where we end up in a bathroom?? and there is a man who stands up. Then looks over at a man in the bed, and then a circle of light with a fetus in it?! what the hell does all that mean.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I can only assume those old men are him, but what, the monolith caused him to age or something?! I'm confused!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||filthyscarecrow||04-02-2001||03:15 PM||||the monoliths aren't there to help anything. they are there as observers/reporters to the civilisation that "planted" life on earth. they monitor life and report back to the "firstborn" as to what's working and what isn't; what needs to be reaped and what needs to be sowed. unfortunately for us, the monolith sent out it's final report just after the 20th century. read the rest of the books. what happened to dave bowman is explained in 2010 and 2061, and what the monoliths are for is explained in 3001: the final odyssey. none of the books are very long, and can be easily read in one night, but they are definitely worth reading...||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||04-02-2001||03:38 PM||||Dave?... what are you doing, Dave?... Dave,<BR>... I'm afraid, Dave...<P>Arthur C. Clarke is a pure genius!  you need to read the complete 2001 set of books.  they are great, however his best book/series was the Rama series.  Those are my favorite books... truly enjoyable!<P>ACC, was/is a visionary of science and space.<P>as for 2001, yes the movie's a little dated, and a bit drrrrrrraaaaawwwwnnnnnnnn ooouuutt.  the monolith is an observer, a watcher, just as filthyscarecrow has said.  as for the old man and the baby, yes that is Dave Bowman.  Read the book and you will understand... they  had to cut out so much, in order to fit it into a movie format.  Dave, goes to visit his mother, also... or was that in 2010?!  <P>hmmmm got me thinking, now!<P>anyway, read the books.... you will understand.<P><BR>hoop||||reg||1
